      "claim": "A cardiac flatline on ECG corresponds to asystole, which is defined as the absence of detectable electrical activity in the heart.",
      "evidence": "ACLS and standard medical textbooks define asystole as a flatline ECG with no measurable electrical activity.",
      "weight": 0.35,
